<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

    <!--
      Deliberately empty.

      The connector is a connection, not an application: a setup key is pasted
      once, two ticks say which channels this database may use, and nobody
      opens it again. It had an app menu of its own, which put a technical
      screen in front of every user and - being the thing that holds the key -
      is the one screen that should not be casually reachable.

      Its actions still exist, so the screens are there for whoever needs them:

        <server>/odoo/action-whatsapp_gateway.action_whatsapp_session
        <server>/odoo/action-whatsapp_gateway.action_whatsapp_message
        <server>/odoo/action-whatsapp_gateway.action_whatsapp_optout
        <server>/odoo/action-whatsapp_gateway.action_whatsapp_config

      The panel prints the first of those on each database's page, next to the
      key it is asking you to paste.

      Day to day, people work in "WhatsApp and Email", which keeps its own
      Messages and Settings.
    -->

</odoo>
